From 1b889c6115bac4c6d9c5003dfde9e7be6714098f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:07:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] aux: no stranger-thread close in
 class_routed_async's to_thread worker or a replaced cache entry

Siblings of the abandoned-provider TLS fd close (hub inbox.db / actions.sqlite3 headers):

1. class_routed_async: adapter clients (Anthropic, Codex, Bedrock, native Gemini) run the sync SDK call on an
   asyncio.to_thread worker. A cancelled await left that worker in SSL_read while the finally closed the
   per-call client from the loop thread; the fd went to the next open() and the worker wrote a TLS alert
   into it. The adapters now use aux_provider_handoff.run_in_thread, which records a still-running worker
   as abandoned in the enclosing client_scope: the loop thread only shuts the sockets down and the worker
   closes both clients after its call returns. A worker cancelled before it started is not recorded.
2. _store_cached_client (Nous 401 refresh) closed the replaced shared entry although another caller can be
   mid-request on it. It now drops it like the FIFO overflow path and _evict_cached_clients.

Repros on a real loopback TLS 1.3 server (tests/agent/test_aux_stranger_close_siblings.py) fail before the
fix with the incident's header b'SQLit\x17\x03\x03\x00\x13...' and pass after.
